  mbl: { ...researchBase, means: 'Many-body localisation is a phase where disorder prevents thermalisation — quantum information persists locally.', explore: 'Disorder, entanglement, and the failure of thermalisation.', what: 'In a disordered interacting system, particles can get stuck — the system never reaches thermal equilibrium, preserving local quantum information.', name: 'MBL — many-body localisation.', physical: 'Distinct from Anderson localisation (non-interacting); MBL includes interactions.', quick: 'Add strong disorder to a quantum system and it may never thermalise — local information persists forever. MBL is a frontier of condensed matter.', physics: 'Entanglement grows logarithmically (not linearly) in MBL.', math: 'Eigenstates are area-law (not volume-law).', equations: [{ eq: 'disorder + interactions → MBL', label: 'Localised phase' }], calculated: ['Entanglement growth', 'Localisation length'], used: 'Quantum memory, condensed matter theory.', observe: 'In MBL, the system remembers its initial state; in thermal, it forgets.', why: 'Disorder + interactions can prevent energy from spreading, locking information in place.', assumptions: ['Strong disorder', 'Interactions'], limitations: ['MBL existence in 2D is debated', 'Finite-size effects'], controls: { 'Disorder (W)': { desc: 'Stronger → more localised.', unit: '—' } }, viz: { 'Entanglement growth': 'Logarithmic in MBL.' } },
